[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I have featured quite a few text-to-speech audio models lately, but considered today\'s drop an absolute bombshell. Fundamentally, it is a voice cloning and speech generation model, but beyond that, it solves the massive headache of needing 10 different tools'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to edit and clean up your audio. It is a complete all-in-one audio powerhouse. We are talking zero-shot voice cloning and instruct-based voice design right out of the gate. But then, the feature list'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'goes crazy. You can do direct speech and lyric content editing, meaning you can type a prompt to add, delete, or replace words right out of a spoken clip, and it blends everything seamlessly. It has'

[00:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'acoustic editing for speed, volume, and pitch control. It has paralinguistic editing, which lets you change a person\'s emotions, strip away heavy accents, or completely swap their vocal'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'timbre. You can even inject non-verbal sounds like a sneeze or a laugh, and convert a normal speaking voice directly into a whisper. Add in full speech enhancement, denoising, and'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'multi-speaker separation, and you literally have every audio tool you could ever need in one single place. It was just released a few hours ago by Tencent. It goes by the name Oak or OAK, and the whole thing is completely open'

[01:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'source. And I am not just hyping this up for no reason. I looked at the research paper they published, and the benchmarks are legit. It is beating state-of-the-art models like the QN3 TTS and C TTS across the board. On the C TTS'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'evaluation, OAK hit a word error rate of 2.65%, which is the lowest error rate out there, while also scoring the highest on speaker similarity. It is completely'

[01:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'destroying the competition in speech editing, too, mostly because older models cannot even do half of what this thing does. Let\'s actually walk through these official examples, so you can hear'

[01:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'what we\'re dealing with live. First up is Instruct TTS, which is basically voice design from a text prompt. Let\'s play this clip. &gt;&gt; You see, my dear, the trap was never meant for you. It was always meant for'

[02:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'him. &gt;&gt; Holy smoke, that sounds incredibly natural. It followed the instructions perfectly and does not sound robotic at all. Next, let\'s check out the zero-shot text-to-speech, which is voice cloning.'

[02:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Here\'s a short input audio of a person talking. &gt;&gt; I survived being swallowed by the dark heart of the universe. So, you lost him a wee bit. Quaint to me. &gt;&gt; And here\'s the cloned output.'

[02:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; If not even light can escape the event horizon, how do you think you\'ll escape me? &gt;&gt; Okay, that is pretty insane. Let\'s check out another example right here. Here\'s the second input.'

[02:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Let me walk you through the steps one more time. &gt;&gt; And here\'s the clone. &gt;&gt; Land is the only thing in the world worth working for, worth fighting for, worth dying for, because it\'s the only thing that lasts. &gt;&gt; I find the quality of that cloning to be'

[03:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'absolutely astonishing. The vocal identity is spot-on. But the voice cloning is just the baseline. The speech content editing is where my mind was totally blown. Imagine you have a'

[03:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'recording and you want to drop a new word into the middle of it. In this example, the person originally says "Mamba out", but the prompt asks to insert the word never.'

[03:26] [scene:talk]
