[13:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'weird shift in pitch. You can also slow it down to half speed just as easily. It even gives you full granular control over energy levels and pitch editing. So, how is Auphonic Arc actually doing'

[13:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'all of this? If we look under the hood, they built this using a multimodal large language model for semantic understanding paired with an audio VAE and a hybrid flow transformer. Think of it like a highly coordinated kitchen.'

[13:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The language model reads the recipe, the VAE preps the raw acoustic ingredients, and the dual stream transformer mixes them all together so the final dish matches the instructions perfectly. They'

[13:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'trained this on over 3 billion audio and instruction pairs, which is exactly why it can handle everything from speech generation to removing a sneeze. The best part is that Tencent actually made'

[14:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the code and the model weights completely open source right now on GitHub and Hugging Face. They released a 1.5 billion parameter base model that uses a 50 hertz VAE and 20 steps for the absolute highest quality. They also'

[14:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'released a superfast distilled flash model that gets near teacher quality in just four steps with absolutely zero classifier free guidance required. Both models sit under 7 GB, though you\'ll'

